 "result": "fibmod.py is a vectorized numpy fast-doubling Fibonacci mod 1e9+7. It parses all inputs into a uint64 array and runs one fast-doubling pass over the bits of the largest value, using np.where to select between the two branches. It passes the sample (in-0 matches out-0 exactly) and is registered by assay with baseline 8.18676 (noise 5.3%). A full run on the 30k-value sample takes about 0.12s wall, most of which is Python and numpy startup, so further gains are likely below noise. I stopped here rather than spend energy on variants that probably would not beat the baseline.",
